  "details": "I am using the \"Senheiser Profile\" microphone, which Windows detects as both a microphone and a speaker, so I’m not sure whether the issue is triggered when the mic side gets unplugged or the speaker side.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1) Join a world that has a working video player, and play a video (tested on USharpVideoPlayer and ProTV), for instance \"Avatar testing chamber\" https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_a5e9ec13-36b1-4e63-ae0c-dab9023401f9/info\n\n2) Unplug the mic/speaker, then plug it back in.\n\n3) World audio and video player audio stop working, but player audio still works\n\nVideo-player audio works again if the video is restarted (AVPro), but world audio stays broken. I assume those audio sources need to be reinitialized as well.\n\nI’m not sure if this is a new bug related to Steam Audio or an older one.\n\nThe screenshot shows my logs.\n\nI don't have any other audio devices plugged into my PC.",
